    "q-132362": {
      "dom_id": "step-q132362",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Given that $X∼\\text{Exp}(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}),$ what is $\\text{Var}[X]?$",
      "worked_solution": "If $X∼\\text{Exp}(\\lambda )$ is an exponential random variable, then\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\frac{1}{{\\lambda }^{2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, for our random variable $X∼\\text{Exp}(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}),$ we have the following variance:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\frac{1}{{(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(\\frac{1}{2})} \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
